Angola,Governance,Angola launches integrated vaccination campaign to protect more than 10 million children,https://afro.who.int/countries/angola/news/angola-launches-integrated-vaccination-campaign-protect-more-10-million-children,WHO | Regional Office for Africa,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Starting today, more than 10 million children across the country will begin receiving vaccinations against polio, measles, rubella, and yellow fever, as part of one of the largest public health operations ever carried out in Angola.","Launched today in Luanda by the Vice President of the Republic, Dr. Esperança Maria Eduardo Francisco da Costa, the National Integrated Vaccination Campaign represents an unprecedented effort by the Angolan government to strengthen children’s protection against potentially deadly diseases, increase herd immunity, and consolidate the country’s progress in the prevention and control of vaccine-preventable diseases.","The campaign will take place from October 23 to 27. It will involve more than 77,000 health professionals, volunteers, social mobilizers, and community leaders, organized into more than 11,000 vaccination teams that will operate in urban communities, rural areas, and hard-to-reach areas across all of the country’s provinces.",yes,no,5,5
