Djibouti,Macroeconomy,Kenya’s 2027/28 Budget Hits KSh 5.42 Trillion as Development Spending Is Cut,https://www.dawan.africa/news/kenyas-202728-budget-hits-ksh-542-trillion-as-development-spending-is-cut,Dawan Africa,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Kenya, October 23, 2026 - The National Treasury has released updated numbers for the 2027/28 financial year, and the picture is clearer , and tighter, than it was two months ago.","The total proposed budget now stands at KSh 5.416 trillion, or 23.6 percent of GDP. That is higher than the KSh 5.323 trillion projected in the earlier Draft Budget Review and Outlook Paper. Recurrent spending is set to cross the KSh 4 trillion mark for the first time, reaching KSh 4.021 trillion. Development spending, however, has been revised downwards from KSh 958 billion to KSh 915.8 billion.","Total revenue is now projected at KSh 4.004 trillion. Ordinary revenue has been pushed up slightly to KSh 3.249 trillion. Even with the higher revenue target, the deficit is expected to widen to KSh 1.353 trillion, or 5.9 percent of GDP.",yes,no,2,8
Djibouti,Macroeconomy,"China, Djibouti say all countries should enjoy freedom of navigation in Red Sea, World News",https://www.asiaone.com/world/us-and-china-form-ai-blocs-countries-are-increasingly-torn-between-them,AsiaOne.com,22 Oct 2026,,no,"HONG KONG — With the two leading AI powers, the US and China, forming their own AI blocs, other countries are manoeuvring to harness the strengths of both groupings and avoid losing out.","As the rivalry intensifies, experts say the window for countries to be able to choose freely between the two AI superpowers may be narrowing, forcing them to at one point pick between the US-led Pax Silica and the China-inspired World AI Cooperation Organisation.","That could put many countries in a dilemma: Do they go with the US's most advanced chips and AI technologies, or join China's more affordable, open-source AI systems?",yes,no,3,7
