Liberia,Agrifood & Climate,"Livelihoods, Innovations, Food Security and Entrepreneurship (LIFE)",https://www.concern.net/knowledge-hub/livelihood-innovations-food-security-and-entrepreneurship-life,Concern Worldwide,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Liberia continues to face high levels of food insecurity, poverty and pressure on rural livelihoods. In 2024, WFP reported that more than 2 million people, around 47% of the population, were food insecure, with many households affected by low agricultural productivity, reliance on imported staple foods and rising prices. The 2025 Global Hunger Index classifies hunger in Liberia as “serious”, with over one-third of the population undernourished.","These challenges are especially important in rural counties such as Grand Bassa and Rivercess, where many households depend on rain-fed smallholder farming and have limited access to markets, finance and services. Strengthening inclusive, nutrition-sensitive and market-oriented livelihoods is therefore key to helping families improve food security, income and resilience..","In response to these challenges, the Livelihoods, Innovations, Food Security and Entrepreneurship (LIFE) programme supports rural households in Grand Bassa and Rivercess to strengthen food security, incomes and resilience. The Irish Aid-funded programme is implemented by Concern Worldwide Liberia from January 2023 to December 2027 under Food Systems for Food Security (FS4FS).",yes,no,1,9
