Mozambique,Macroeconomy,Mozambique parliament adds $56mn of gas revenue to 2026 budget,https://www.intellinews.com/mozambique-parliament-adds-56mn-of-gas-revenue-to-2026-budget-478611/?source=mozambique,IntelliNews,25 Oct 2026,,no,"Mozambique’s parliament approved a MZN3.5746bn ($55.9mn) increase to the 2026 state budget on October 24, allocating previously collected natural gas revenues to roads, flood recovery, damaged public buildings and a parliamentary complex amid opposition concerns over spending priorities and implementation deadlines.","The amendment to the Economic and Social Plan and State Budget (PESOE) passed by 164 votes to 62 during an extraordinary session in Maputo attended by 226 of the 250 deputies. The governing Frelimo party supported the measure, while Podemos, Renamo and the Democratic Movement of Mozambique (MDM) opposed it, Diário Económico reported on October 25, citing Portuguese news agency Lusa .","The revision incorporates unspent Rovuma Basin gas revenues carried forward from the previous financial year and held in the transitional account of Mozambique’s sovereign wealth fund. It does not represent additional gas revenue collected in 2026. The amendment more than doubles the oil and gas revenue allocated to the 2026 budget, to MZN6.518bn from MZN2.9434bn, according to details released by parliament’s standing committee and reported by Notícias .",yes,no,1,9
