Mozambique,Digital Economy,Paratus deploys Starlink to Zambian schools,https://www.connectingafrica.com/connectivity/paratus-deploys-starlink-to-zambian-schools,Connecting Africa,19 Oct 2026,,no,"Connectivity solutions provider Paratus Zambia has successfully deployed Starlink Internet services to 18 schools in Lusaka, providing Internet access to more than 10,000 learners.","According to the company, the connectivity rollout was completed in approximately two weeks, replacing an unstable network that was prone to frequent outages and constrained by limited infrastructure.","""With traditional connectivity options often constrained by distance from cellular towers and reliance on fixed-line infrastructure, Paratus Zambia has, through this project using Starlink, now enabled fast, stable Internet access across all Family Legacy sites with minimal ground infrastructure and rapid deployment,"" Paratus Zambia said in a statement.",yes,no,1,9
