Nigeria,Jobs & Employment,Okpanachi: Nigeria’s Investment Drive to Create Millions of Decent Jobs,https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/10/17/okpanachi-nigerias-investment-drive-to-create-millions-of-decent-jobs/,THISDAYLIVE,25 Oct 2026,,no,"Managing Director of the Development Bank of Nigeria, Tony Okpanachi, says expanding finance for micro, small and medium-sized enterprises could unlock millions of quality jobs. Speaking at the IMF/World Bank Annual Meetings in Bangkok, Thailand, he discusses investment, access to finance, global development models and partnerships. Nume Ekeghe presents excerpts","What have been the major outcomes of your engagements at the IMF/World Bank Annual Meetings, particularly for the Development Bank of Nigeria?","et me start by saying the theme of the Annual Meetings is quite apt, given the fact that the issue of job creation is quite important, especially for developing countries and Nigeria in particular. There have been a lot of issues around unemployment, the youthful population, the entrepreneurial population, and the need to be able to get great jobs, not only jobs, but decent jobs. The second thing, which is quite important here, is the opportunity Nigeria had to showcase the reforms and the changes in Nigeria. Expectations are looking up in Nigeria. We had this investors’ forum where the Minister of Finance and Coordinating Minister of the Economy and the Central Bank Governor were also present to share with the Western community what Nigeria is doing and the results of the reforms. We can see that even globally, the World Bank and the IMF are acknowledging that Nigeria is on the right track. So, i must say it was a very important opportunity to showcase Nigeria.",yes,no,3,7
