Nigeria,Governance,"Uzodimma: media freedom, economic independence key to Nigeria’s democracy",https://thenationonlineng.net/uzodimma-media-freedom-economic-independence-key-to-nigerias-democracy/,The Nation Newspaper,26 Oct 2026,,no,"Imo State Governor Hope Uzodimma has identified economic vulnerability, proprietorial interference and censorship as major threats to media independence, warning that failure to address them could undermine journalism’s credibility and Nigeria’s democratic development.","Uzodimma said the media had played a significant role in deepening democracy and accelerating national development since the return to democratic governance in 1999, but stressed that journalists must be protected from pressures capable of compromising their professional responsibilities.","The governor spoke in Abuja at the weekend while delivering the third Raymond Aleogho Dokpesi Annual Diamond Lecture, with the theme, “Media, Democratic Consolidation and Development”.",yes,no,4,6
