Nigeria,Agrifood & Climate,"Nigeria’s floods killed 245 people, displaced over 200,000, says NEMA",https://gazettengr.com/nigerias-floods-killed-245-people-displaced-over-200000-says-nema/,Peoples Gazette Nigeria,23 Oct 2026,,no,"NEMA said flooding affected 673,350 people across 134 local government areas in 28 states, displacing 214,997 and killing 245 as of October 20.","The National Emergency Management Agency (NEMA) said flooding affected 673,350 people across 134 local government areas in 28 states, displacing 214,997 and killing 245 as of October 20.","NEMA’s director-general, Zubaida Umar, disclosed this at the National Emergency Coordination Forum on Thursday in Abuja. Ms Umar said the country was confronting interconnected challenges of flooding, cholera and Ebola.",yes,no,2,8
Nigeria,Agrifood & Climate,Onuigbo: Nigeria Has Covered Great Mileage in Energy Transition,https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/10/25/onuigbo-nigeria-has-covered-great-mileage-in-energy-transition/,THISDAYLIVE,25 Oct 2026,,no,"President of Global Legislators Organisation for Better Environment (GLOBE) Legislators International, Hon.Sam Onuigbo has said that Nigeria has attained great milestones in the area of energy transition and climate sustainability under President Bola Tinubu.","Onuigbo, who is also the sponsor of Nigeria’s signature climate change law, made the remarks while being honoured with Fellowship of the Solar Energy Society of Nigeria (FSESN) in recognition of his contributions to Climate Change action and advocacy. He also observed the commendable and focused attention of the governors of Nasarawa, Lagos, Kaduna, Katsina, and Borno states towards energy transition and carbon market initiatives.","The former lawmaker noted that if governments at the subnational level emulate the concerted actions of the Federal Government, Nigeria would emerge as a leading voice in environmental sustainability.",yes,no,3,7
