Tanzania,Workforce & Human Capital,Class Consciousness: A tool for human rights,https://www.industriall-union.org/class-consciousness-tanzania-young-workers,industriall-union,22 Oct 2026,,no,"22 October, 2026 Twenty-six young workers, including 16 women, met in Dar es Salaam on 20-22 October 2026. They examined how working class consciousness can strengthen union strategies to defend workers’ rights.","The fifth youth activist school, supported by FES Tanzania, NITO and STRYKE, linked political analysis with human rights due diligence. This included identifying, preventing and addressing abuses in workplaces and supply chains.","Participants included IndustriALL affiliates Tanzania Mines Energy and Construction Union (TAMICO) and Tanzania Union of Industrial and Commercial Workers (TUICO). BWI affiliate Tanzania Plantation and Allied Workers Union (TPAWU) joined via the partnership with IndustriALL’s African regional office. Likewise, Zanzibar Public Services Workers Union (ZAPSWU) and Vibindo Society participated from the labour movement and civil society.",yes,no,0,10
