Burundi,Jobs & Employment,"Catholic Church in Burundi Supporting Over 80,000 Congolese Refugees",https://www.aciafrica.org/news/24895/catholic-church-in-burundi-supporting-over-80000-congolese-refugees,ACI Africa,23 Oct 2026,Refugees,no,"The Catholic Church in Burundi is working with humanitarian organizations to support more than 80,000 refugees from the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), the Local Ordinary of the Catholic Diocese of Bururi has said.","A Thursday, October 22, report by Agenzia Fides quotes Bishop Salvator Niciteretse , who is the coordinator of the International Forum of Catholic Action (FIAC) for Africa, saying that most of the refugees come from Uvira, the capital of South Kivu Province in eastern DRC.","The conflict in eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) has roots stretching back to the 1994 genocide in neighbouring Rwanda, which drove large numbers of refugees, including former combatants, into the Congolese provinces of North Kivu and South Kivu.",yes,no,0,10
