Burundi,Digital Economy,Burundi Signs $1.4bn Power PPP With Weza Power,https://uchumi360.com/r/b/burundi-signs-billion-power,Uchumi360,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Burundi has signed a 25 year US$1.4 billion electricity distribution concession with Weza Power that aims to add more than 1.2 million household and business connections and 52,000 kilometres of network infrastructure. The programme addresses a distribution funding gap already identified in Burundi’s National Energy Compact, but much of the capital still has to be mobilised through grants, concessional finance and private investment.","Burundi has signed a 25 year electricity distribution concession with Weza Power that aims to mobilise US$1.4 billion, build or upgrade approximately 52,000 kilometres of distribution lines and connect more than 1.2 million households and businesses, placing private capital at the centre of one of Africa’s least electrified countries’ attempt to turn recent increases in power generation into electricity that can actually reach consumers. The agreement was signed on October 15 between the government and Weza Power, an Anzana Electric Group company, and divides distribution responsibilities between the new private operator and state utility REGIDESO, which will retain the national transmission network and continue distributing electricity in roughly half of the country.","The project is unusually large relative to Burundi’s existing electricity system. Weza Power says the concession is intended to provide first time or improved access to about eight million people and raise on grid electrification above 50 percent, while the government’s own National Energy Compact identifies distribution as the single largest funding requirement in its electricity expansion programme. The compact estimates that Burundi needs about US$1.64 billion for distribution infrastructure alone by 2030, compared with US$700 million for generation and US$200 million for transmission, meaning the Weza concession corresponds closely with an investment deficit the government had already quantified before the final PPP was signed.",yes,no,3,7
