Burundi,Workforce & Human Capital,"Burundi : in Gitega, a shortage of drinking water plunges boarding schools into a health and academic crisis",https://www.sosmediasburundi.org/en/2026/10/22/burundi-in-gitega-a-shortage-of-drinking-water-plunges-boarding-schools-into-a-health-and-academic-crisis/,SOS Médias Burundi,22 Oct 2026,,no,"Gitega, October 22, 2026 — A lack of drinking water in boarding schools in Gitega—located in central Burundi and home to the country’s political capital—is disrupting studies and compromising hygiene conditions for pupils. At the Christ-Roi Technical High School in Mushasha and the Gitega High School, more than 1,800 pupils are struggling with water supply issues. Pupils and administration authorities at both institutions fear an outbreak of diseases linked to poor hygiene and are calling on the authorities to find a sustainable solution.","“We no longer have time to review the material learned in class. For instance, the 3:00 p.m. study session has been scrapped because we have to go fetch water from developed springs around the city of Gitega,” laments 18-year-old Générose Kanyamuneza, a third-year pupil in the Banking and Insurance track at the Christ-Roi Technical High School in Mushasha.","She explains that the water they collect is used primarily for preparing evening meals, which comes at the expense of time that should be dedicated to their studies.",yes,no,3,7
