Cameroon,Jobs & Employment,Remarks by CDA John G. Robinson – Cameroon International Tech Summit (CITS26),https://cm.usembassy.gov/freedom-250-independence-day-remarks-by-charge-daffaires-a-i-john-g-robinson/,U.S. Embassy in Cameroon (.gov),20 Oct 2026,,no,"Your Excellency the Minister Delegate to the Minister of External Relations in charge of Cooperation with the Commonwealth, members of the Cameroonian government, traditional authorities, members of the diplomatic corps, business leaders, representatives of academia, civil society, and other distinguished guests,","Good evening, and welcome to everyone here with us tonight, and to those joining us online from across Cameroon and beyond.  This evening we celebrate the 250th anniversary of American independence, declared on July 4, 1776. Throughout this year, we are marking this milestone through a series of events we call Freedom 250 .  It is a privilege to celebrate this historic anniversary with you.","Two hundred and fifty years ago, America’s founders declared that all people possess certain unalienable rights:  life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness. Those ideals have inspired generations of Americans while reminding us that freedom is never finished; it must be renewed by each generation.",yes,no,2,8
