Guinea,Jobs & Employment,"Marape orders economic taskforce to curb overspending, lift revenue",https://islandsbusiness.com/news-break/marape-orders-economic-taskforce-to-curb-overspending-lift-revenue/,Islands Business,26 Oct 2026,,no,"PRIME Minister James Marape has ordered Papua New Guinea’s economic leadership to shift its focus from public spending to raising revenue through a stronger non-resource sector, setting targets for a K200 billion economy by 2030 and K500 billion by 2050.","Marape delivered the directive at Melanesian House during the rollout of the Growth and Economic Reform National Coordinating Committee (GER-NCC), a cross-agency body intended to cut bureaucratic red tape and speed up structural economic reforms.","“Everything else you hear today, if you forget, go away with these two numbers K200 billion economy, K50 billion budget…minimum starting point,” Marape said, referring to a current K140 billion economy and a proposed K50 billion national budget.",yes,no,2,8
