Libya,Macroeconomy,"""Libya cannot remain a corridor for illegal migration"": Trump",https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/international/3997070-libya-cannot-remain-a-corridor-for-illegal-migration-trump,Devdiscourse,26 Oct 2026,,no,"US President Donald Trump praised the resilience of the Libyan people and their counter-terrorism cooperation with Washington, while firmly asserting that the North African nation must immediately cease serving as a primary transit route for illegal migration. In a statement shared on Truth Social, Trump highlighted the shared sacrifices between the two nations in combating extremist elements, pointing to past joint efforts against ISIS.","""The Libyan people are proud, resilient, hospitable, and deserving of peace and prosperity. The United States and Libya share a strong and enduring partnership in combating terrorism, building on our historic success in defeating ISIS in Libya together,"" Trump stated. However, emphasising the urgent need to address unchecked migration flows across the Mediterranean, the US President called for decisive action.","""We respect the Libyan people and the sacrifices that brave Libyans made fighting ISIS, the common enemy of both our peoples, but Libya cannot remain a corridor for illegal migration, and this must end now,"" he said. Underlining Washington's backing for Libya's democratic roadmap, Trump reaffirmed US support for consolidating state governance and holding overdue national polls to resolve the country's longstanding political division.",yes,no,2,8
