Mauritania,Macroeconomy,Aura aims for final investment decision on Mauritania project this year,https://world-nuclear-news.org/articles/fid-sees-etango-enter-full-scale-construction,World Nuclear News,20 Oct 2026,,no,"The Etango project is in the Erongo Region of Namibia, 30 kilometres south-east of Swakopmund, with an estimated mineral resource base of 207 million pounds U3O8 (79,622 tU) at a 100 ppm cut-off.","The final investment decision (FID) has been taken by the Etango Joint Venture (Bannerman 55%, CNNC Overseas Limited 45%) which holds a 95% interest in the project. Bannerman gifted a 5% loan-carried shareholding in Etango to Namibian social welfare organisation the One Economy Foundation in 2017. CNNC Overseas Limited (CNOL) is a subsidiary of China National Uranium Corporation and part of China National Nuclear Corporation (CNNC).","“Today's FID by the Etango JV is a defining moment for Bannerman, for our partner, CNOL, and for Namibia,"" Bannerman Managing Director and CEO Gavin Chamberlain said. ""It is the culmination of more than two decades of exploration, study and disciplined de-risking,and it formally commits the JV to full-scale construction of the world-class Etango Uranium Project. With construction fully funded on a debt-free basis, a Tier-1 strategic partner in CNOL and a cornerstone offtake framework on market-based terms, Etango is now set to become the next major greenfield uranium project globally to enter production.""",yes,no,0,10
Mauritania,Macroeconomy,Aura Energy's Tiris Uranium Project: $500M Mauritania Mine Advances - News and Statistics,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxPQVlpNXFGRV9OY2kzWTBCZlRWR01Jcl8wd3Y0ZHJsdUZybzFqN05LQm40WDRZVmZLdU9PX2I0MWl5dTczb3p0UFRGR0lpTnVRWFMwb2NhejRDQlRFZ3VFZnItNGdqOFF0bGcwejRqMjhmMWRwdkxfQWVnbHdfUmZaVUFzOHRYajNQdVZJY2tGdVNXSzNsemsza0VhbjgydzVhS2FiQnREaG9TVFRsbGN5ZldTVDVET2pFYkE?oc=5,IndexBox,20 Oct 2026,,no,,,,no,yes,1,7
Mauritania,Macroeconomy,"Mauritania’s first uranium mine comes into view despite funding, security issues",https://www.mining.com/mauritanias-first-uranium-mine-comes-into-view-despite-funding-security-issues/,Mining.com,20 Oct 2026,,no,"Aura Energy (ASX: AEE; AIM: AURA) is moving closer to building Mauritania’s first uranium mine after a bankable feasibility study outlined a $500-million valuation for its Tiris project, despite a 52% increase in construction costs to $350 million.","The study gives Tiris a post-tax internal rate of return (IRR) of 28%, 11 percentage points lower than in a technical report from 2024, even though the uranium price assumption rose 12% to $90 per pound. Tiris is about 1,100 km northeast of the capital Nouakchott, located in the mineral-rich but high-risk Tiris Zemmour region.","“The army manages security [there] and has cleared artisanal miners from a 10-km strip along the Algerian frontier,” Sean Hagarty, security analyst and founder of the risk intelligence firm Region Alert told The Northern Miner on Tuesday.",yes,no,2,8
