Mauritania,Governance,"West Africa risks authoritarian rule as democracy weakens, Nigerian judge warns",https://thenationonlineng.net/west-africa-risks-authoritarian-rule-as-democracy-weakens-nigerian-judge-warns/,The Nation Newspaper,23 Oct 2026,,no,"A Nigerian judge, Justice George Chibueze Nnamani, has warned that growing executive dominance, weakening democratic institutions and public disillusionment with governance could push West Africa towards authoritarian rule, calling for urgent measures to safeguard judicial independence and constitutional democracy.","Nnamani, President of the Enugu State Customary Court of Appeal, also expressed concern over the resurgence of military rule in parts of the sub-region, questioning whether it reflected renewed military ambition or growing frustration with the performance of civilian administrations.","He spoke while delivering the keynote address at the fourth edition of the Civil Society Week for West Africa (CSWWA 2026), organised by Spaces for Change (S4C) West Africa and its partners in Enugu. The two-day conference, held at Hotel Presidential, has the theme, “Strengthening Judicial Protection of Civic Space in West Africa.”",yes,no,1,9
