Sahel,Macroeconomy,ECOWAS and Sahel states seek new trade rules after political split,https://www.intellinews.com/ecowas-and-sahel-states-seek-new-trade-rules-after-political-split-477069/?source=benin,IntelliNews,20 Oct 2026,,no,"The Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS) and the Confederation of Sahel States (AES) have agreed to establish joint working groups to negotiate their future relationship, as the two blocs seek to reconcile a political separation with economic ties that remain deeply entrenched.","At a ministerial meeting in Dakar on October 17, the two sides agreed that the groups would conduct technical negotiations towards a framework co-operation agreement. Their conclusions will be submitted to ministers before another meeting, whose date and venue have yet to be decided.","Senegal’s foreign ministry described the talks as the first foreign minister-level meeting between ECOWAS and the AES since Burkina Faso, Mali and Niger, all led by military governments, formally withdrew from the regional bloc on January 29, 2025, reducing its membership from 15 countries to 12.",yes,no,3,7
