Sahel,Workforce & Human Capital,Algeria-Niger ‘security pact’: What’s behind Algiers’ military push into the Sahel?,https://www.theafricareport.com/434371/algeria-niger-security-pact-whats-behind-algiers-military-push-into-the-sahel/,The Africa Report,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Algeria, encouraged by Russia, is strengthening ties with the Alliance of Sahel States (AES) . On 21 October, Niger’s Minister of State for National Defence, Salifou Mody, visited Algiers for the second time in two weeks.","He met President Abdelmadjid Tebboune and signed a loosely defined “security pact” with Saïd Chengriha, Chief of Staff of l’Armée Nationale Populaire (ANP). The terms of the agreement have not been made public.","Chengriha said the Algerian army was “ready” to consider any proposal from Niger to strengthen military cooperation , while Mody praised the “level of coordination” between the two armed forces. Neither side disclosed concrete details of the memorandum of understanding.",yes,no,3,12
