Benin,Jobs & Employment,Expert harps on increased job chances despite advent of AI technology at computing graduates induction,https://nigerianobservernews.com/2026/10/expert-harps-on-increased-job-chances-despite-advent-of-ai-technology-at-computing-graduates-induction/,The Nigerian Observer,23 Oct 2026,,no,"BENIN CITY: A computer expert and immediate past Vice Chancellor of Kiagbodo University in Delta State Professor Chinye Chiemeke has allayed fears of possible job loses globally on account of evolving computing technology, saying that for every job eliminated, two new ones are created.","Prof Chiemeke spoke at the 3rd induction and oath taking ceremony of graduates of computing from Wellspring University, Benin City on Wednesday amidst global fears of machines taking over jobs from humans and the attendant consequences on families.","The former Vice Chancellor whose lecture was titled: Beyond the Certificate in Building a Future-Ready Career Through Professionalism, Innovation, and Life-Long Learning, said that in as much as the fears are real, the corresponding opportunities created by the new technologies in the area of jobs creation, far out number those that would be lost.",yes,no,3,7
