Egypt,Workforce & Human Capital,"Egypt Forum 2026 outlines sweeping development agenda to raise living standards, boost growth",https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxOcW1XcWpPaGR1VVpaNW16Y3k4bHJPN3RzZWJrVC1COV9iSjg2WnEyQnlwVmQxS2VOTWV2QzZvaEoxcVIxMWtmcUtPU2QzcHJoY0g1MTJYbDZ5d0U2VE5yRGlEZE80bXpjVmNlSEdrXzVsVVIxMGU3VUhmUnpBVDRvTXpnNmhrSVltSUpuOVJOR1ZKd1F6SDZDdzdnNHFjRV9HOW13RTIwWEFVdl9FNGpEWXRvaw?oc=5,Egypt Today,24 Oct 2026,,no,,,,no,yes,4,4
Egypt,Workforce & Human Capital,Egypt’s PM Warns Arabic Language Decline Poses National Security Threat,https://egyptianstreets.com/2026/10/22/egypts-pm-warns-arabic-language-decline-poses-national-security-threat/,Egyptian Streets,22 Oct 2026,,no,"Egyptian Prime Minister Mostafa Madbouly has warned that students’ inability to speak Arabic proficiently poses a serious challenge to Egypt’s national identity and national security, calling for greater attention to Arabic-language education in international schools.","Speaking during the Egypt 2026 Forum on Monday, Madbouly questioned whether students enrolled in international schools had sufficient command of Arabic, describing it as the national language and the language of Egyptian society. He argued that the issue extends beyond education policy to the preservation of Egypt’s cultural identity and national security.","Madbouly’s remarks came during a session titled “What Are Our Children Learning, and Does It Prepare Them for the Future?” The discussion addressed concerns raised by parents about the teaching of Arabic and religious education in international schools, as well as whether grades in these subjects should count toward students’ overall academic results.",yes,no,5,5
