Gambia,Macroeconomy,"Coalition 2026 unveils 3 pillars, 13 policies, 66 actions to transform Gambia by 2031",https://thepoint.gm/africa/gambia/headlines/coalition-2026-unveils-3-pillars-13-policies-66-actions-to-transform-gambia-by-2031,The Point Newspaper,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Coalition 2026, led by UNITE leader Talib Ahmed Bensouda, has unveiled its manifesto titled ‘The Gambia We Deserve’, outlining 3 pillars, 13 policy points and 66 priority actions it says will be completed by 2031 when The Gambia turns 66 years old.","Speaking at the launch on October 22, 2026, ahead of the December presidential election, Bensouda said the manifesto is built around governance and trust, human development and economic integrity, simplified into three commitments of trust, people and prosperity. The plan includes a constitutional review and referendum within two years, raising health spending to 15% of the budget, and establishing a National Development Bank to drive job creation and economic growth.","Bensouda said the plan includes 3 pillars, 13 policy points and 66 priority actions, explaining that the figure aligns with The Gambia’s age in 2031.",yes,no,1,9
