Gambia,Macroeconomy,Finance minister to present 2027 budget of D66.78B today,https://thepoint.gm/africa/gambia/headlines/finance-minister-to-present-2027-budget-of-d66-78b-today,The Point Newspaper,23 Oct 2026,,no,"The Minister of Finance and Economic Affairs is expected to lay the final 2027 national budget before the National Assembly today , with initial estimates putting government spending at D66.78 billion, a 12.5 per cent increase from the D59.36 billion approved for 2026.","The proposed budget, which has already undergone scrutiny by the Assembly’s Finance and Public Accounts Committee (FPAC), includes recommendations from the committee ahead of the minister’s presentation of the final estimates for the 2027 fiscal year.","The initial estimates show that debt servicing will remain the single largest claim on government-funded expenditure, with D16.17 billion earmarked for national debt obligations. The allocation represents roughly one-third of the D48.6 billion expected to be financed directly by the government.",yes,no,3,7
Gambia,Macroeconomy,"Gambia's rice cheaper than Senegal, Liberia, Guinea, Minister Bah claims",https://thepoint.gm/africa/gambia/headlines/gambias-rice-cheaper-than-senegal-liberia-guinea-minister-bah-claims,The Point Newspaper,21 Oct 2026,,no,"Lands Minister Hamat Bah says a bag of rice in The Gambia is cheaper than in Senegal, Guinea-Conakry, Liberia, Sierra Leone and Guinea-Bissau, insisting the Barrow government has cut living costs despite public outcry.","Speaking in Banjul on October 19 at the final meeting of President Barrow's Meet the People Tour, Bah said rice prices have fallen from D2,200 to between D1,650 and D1,700 due to government interventions.","""There is a message circulating that cost of living is high. There are some things Gambians must know,"" he said.",yes,no,4,6
