Gambia,Agrifood & Climate,FAO DIRECTOR-GENERAL HONOURS AWA JAGNE AT GLOBAL 100 WOMEN HEROES EVENT IN ROME,https://www.fao.org/newsroom/detail/fao-honours-100-women-heroes-driving-change-across-agrifood-systems/en,Food and Agriculture Organization,19 Oct 2026,Women,no,"Rome – The Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO) today honoured 100 Women Heroes in Agrifood Systems and Rural Development , recognizing women from around the world whose work is making a difference across agrifood systems and rural communities.","The initiative was launched by FAO to mark the International Year of the Woman Farmer 2026 . The event also coincides with the International Day of Rural Women celebrated annually on 15 October, to recognize the critical role and contribution of rural women in agriculture and rural development, food security and the eradication of rural poverty.","Opening the presentation ceremony at FAO headquarters in Rome, Director-General QU Dongyu paid tribute to the women being recognized and recalled the influence of his own grandmother, who raised him in a small village in China and taught him how to farm and cook, as well as the value of hard work, resilience and respect for the land.",yes,no,2,8
Gambia,Agrifood & Climate,"National Bakers Union calls for modernisation to strengthen industry, food security",https://thepoint.gm/africa/gambia/national-news/national-bakers-union-calls-for-modernisation-to-strengthen-industry-food-security,The Point Newspaper,22 Oct 2026,,no,"The National Bakers Union of The Gambia (NBUG) has called for stronger collaboration between governments, industry stakeholders and technical partners to modernise Africa's bakery sector, improve production standards and reduce reliance on imported wheat flour.","The call was made by Lamin Dibba, Secretary General of the National Bakers Union of The Gambia and Organising Secretary of the African Bakery and Pastry Association, during the Flour Rising Africa regional workshop held in Dakar, Senegal, from 13 to 14 October 2026.","The workshop, organised by Mühlenchemie and DeutscheBack, brought together millers, bakers, pasta manufacturers, scientists, equipment suppliers and other industry experts from across the continent to discuss innovations in flour processing, baking technology, food security and professional training.",yes,no,3,7
