Lesotho,Governance,Sentebale reportedly pauses action against Prince Harry after recording 20% income drop,https://www.civilsociety.co.uk/news/sentebale-reportedly-pauses-action-against-prince-harry-after-recording-20-per-cent-income-drop.html,Civil Society Media,20 Oct 2026,,no,"Sentebale is reportedly pausing its legal action against Prince Harry, as recently published accounts show a near-20% drop in income.","Financial statements published last week show the charity’s total income fell to £2.024m last year, as a regulatory compliance case “increased governance and reputational exposure”.","In February 2025, Sentebale, which was founded in 2006 by Harry and Prince Seeiso of Lesotho and supports children and young people in southern Africa, raised governance-related concerns with the Charity Commission following an internal dispute.",yes,no,2,8
