Mauritius,Macroeconomy,India’s Monopoly in Mauritius: A Satellite State in the Making?,https://www.geopoliticalmonitor.com/indias-monopoly-in-mauritius-a-satellite-state-in-the-making/,Geopolitical Monitor,23 Oct 2026,,no,"The chief of India’s navy visited Mauritius from August 10 to 13, meeting Prime Minister Navinchandra Ramgoolam and pledging continued Indian support for the capabilities of the Mauritius Police Force and National Coast Guard. Four days later, the fourth cohort of senior Mauritian civil servants began a training program at India’s National Centre for Good Governance in New Delhi, part of an agreement to train 500 Mauritian officials over five years.","Within eight days, India was shaping both the island’s maritime security and the formation of its bureaucracy. No other partner operates at comparable depth across defense, capital flows, bureaucratic capacity, and diplomacy, and the pattern raises a question with implications for the wider Indian Ocean: whether Mauritius is becoming a state whose strategic choices are effectively made in New Delhi.","The relationship rests on demographic foundations without parallel in Africa. More than 70 percent of the 1.2 million Mauritians trace ancestry to India, a legacy of indentured migration under British rule that sustains ties across every Mauritian government.",yes,no,3,7
Mauritius,Macroeconomy,Mauritius lifts curfew following days of unrest,https://travelmole.com/news/mauritius-lifts-curfew,TravelMole,20 Oct 2026,,no,"Mauritius has lifted a nighttime curfew following a wave of violent protests, but the unrest could test the Indian Ocean island’s tourism industry as it heads into the crucial year-end holiday season .","The turmoil in Mauritius began around October 7, 2026 , with protests over water shortages and the rising cost of living, according to reports.","The situation escalated on October 9, when a police officer shot and wounded a 27-year-old woman, triggering more violent demonstrations. Protests, roadblocks and property damage intensified over the following days, prompting authorities to impose a nighttime curfew on October 13.",yes,no,4,6
