Congo Brazzaville,Macroeconomy,"Congo Brazzaville Moves to Drop Visas for Africans, But an ETA Will Still Apply",https://katakenya.org/congo-brazzaville-moves-to-drop-visas-for-africans-but-an-eta-will-still-apply/,Kenya Association of Travel Agents,25 Oct 2026,,no,"The Republic of the Congo has moved a significant step closer to opening its borders to fellow Africans, after the cabinet approved a bill on 14 October that would scrap visa requirements for African nationals from 1 January 2027 . For the regional travel trade, it is a development worth watching closely, though one that comes with an important caveat attached.","The legislation gives legal shape to a promise made by President Denis Sassou N’Guesso during Africa Day celebrations on 25 May. That announcement placed Brazzaville alongside a growing group of African governments dismantling the visa walls that have long made travel within the continent more complicated than travelling to Europe. It is worth stating plainly that this concerns the Republic of the Congo , with its capital at Brazzaville, and not the neighbouring Democratic Republic of the Congo, a distinction that regularly trips up even experienced consultants.","Cabinet approval, however, is not the finish line. Parliament must still examine and adopt the bill before anything changes at the border. Until that process concludes, the current entry rules remain in force, and agencies should continue advising clients accordingly rather than selling a future that has not yet arrived.",yes,no,0,10
