Eritrea,Macroeconomy,Kenya’s 2027/28 Budget Hits KSh 5.42 Trillion as Development Spending Is Cut,https://www.dawan.africa/news/kenyas-202728-budget-hits-ksh-542-trillion-as-development-spending-is-cut,Dawan Africa,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Kenya, October 23, 2026 - The National Treasury has released updated numbers for the 2027/28 financial year, and the picture is clearer , and tighter, than it was two months ago.","The total proposed budget now stands at KSh 5.416 trillion, or 23.6 percent of GDP. That is higher than the KSh 5.323 trillion projected in the earlier Draft Budget Review and Outlook Paper. Recurrent spending is set to cross the KSh 4 trillion mark for the first time, reaching KSh 4.021 trillion. Development spending, however, has been revised downwards from KSh 958 billion to KSh 915.8 billion.","Total revenue is now projected at KSh 4.004 trillion. Ordinary revenue has been pushed up slightly to KSh 3.249 trillion. Even with the higher revenue target, the deficit is expected to widen to KSh 1.353 trillion, or 5.9 percent of GDP.",yes,no,4,6
