Guinea-Bissau,Workforce & Human Capital,Nebraska Ambassadors Forum to explore the changing nature of American diplomacy,https://news.unl.edu/article/nebraska-ambassadors-forum-to-explore-the-changing-nature-of-american-diplomacy,Nebraska Today,20 Oct 2026,,no,"The Nebraska Ambassadors Forum will return to the University of Nebraska–Lincoln on Oct. 27, bringing together four distinguished diplomatic practitioners to examine the enduring role of American diplomacy and how it has evolved to meet a changing world under the theme, “Older than the Nation: The Changing Nature of American Diplomacy.”","The University of Nebraska–Lincoln is partnering with Burlington Capital and the American Academy of Diplomacy to host this year’s event. The 2026 program will feature a public forum followed by a Global Café event, giving students an opportunity to engage directly with the visiting diplomats.","The public forum will take place from 12:30 to 2 p.m. Oct. 27 in the Nebraska Union's Swanson Auditorium. The event is open to the public, and registration is required to attend.",yes,no,3,7
