Guinea-Bissau,Workforce & Human Capital,Guinea-Bissau stops controversial US-funded vaccine trial on newborns,https://punchng.com/guinea-bissau-stops-controversial-us-funded-vaccine-trial-on-newborns/,Punch Newspapers,22 Oct 2026,,no,"The government of Guinea-Bissau has halted a controversial United States-backed study that planned to investigate the effects of administering the hepatitis B vaccine to newborns, following international criticism over its ethics.","The lead researcher, Danish scientist Frederik Schaltz-Buchholzer, confirmed the development on Wednesday, saying the project would no longer proceed in the West African country because the necessary government approval had not been granted.","According to The Guardian UK, which reported the development, the proposed study was expected to receive $1.6m from the United States Centres for Disease Control and Prevention, alongside another $1.6m from private donors, including the Pershing Square Foundation and the Bluebell Foundation.",yes,no,6,9
