Morocco,Macroeconomy,Morocco's annual inflation rises to 0.5% in September,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxNaUJYdmNVbnkybFJfYTNYRnROZU01YTBCMVg3a05iQWRjUVpFenpzb05KTVZic0IzNnQzSENLY012TWlWbVczXzJpejZFSndNRldIcV81T0dXdUJJeGRhUmt5VGV0bld2cG9Ic3hpcnhDYXlORVhpS1lULVNYc1lzUkNySHVWYnI2cHQxWG4tRUlEaW42ZTNZcnRfYlEwa1JKZmFxT0V6amI?oc=5,marketscreener.com,22 Oct 2026,,no,,,,no,yes,4,4
Morocco,Macroeconomy,"Why Morocco's Interest Rate Reforms Are Working Better but Still Falling Short, According to IMF",https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/other/3997060-why-moroccos-interest-rate-reforms-are-working-better-but-still-falling-short-according-to-imf,Devdiscourse,25 Oct 2026,,no,"Morocco's monetary policy reforms are beginning to strengthen the country's ability to control inflation, influence bank lending and maintain economic stability, although significant structural challenges continue to limit their effectiveness. A new study by researchers Nadia Mounir and Hannah Brown from the International Monetary Fund (IMF), Middle East and Central Asia Department, examines how monetary policy has evolved following major financial and institutional reforms. Published in October 2026, the research analyzes economic data from 2006 to 2025 and finds that interest rate decisions now have a stronger impact on economic growth and consumer prices than before 2018. However, their effects remain slower and weaker than those observed in many other emerging economies.","The study reveals that Morocco's central bank, Bank Al-Maghrib, has become more effective in influencing economic activity through interest rate decisions. Following reforms introduced since 2018, an unexpected one-percentage-point increase in the policy interest rate reduces economic output by approximately 0.3 percent and inflation by around 0.12 percent.","Before the reforms, the same monetary tightening reduced output by only 0.1 percent and inflation by approximately 0.05 percent. This improvement suggests that changes in borrowing costs are now having a greater influence on economic activity and consumer prices.",yes,no,5,5
Morocco,Digital Economy,"Where Continents Meet, Opportunity Begins",https://www.forbesafrica.com/africa-undiscovered/2026/10/20/where-continents-meet-opportunity-begins,Forbes Africa,20 Oct 2026,,no,"Tunisia’s talent, technology, and industrial strength redefine its role in the global economy.","Tunisia has spent decades being described by where it sits. What defines it now is who lives there. A new generation of engineers, entrepreneurs, researchers, and industrial leaders is turning the country’s historic Mediterranean advantage into something more valuable: a place where ideas are developed, technologies are tested, and expertise travels beyond borders.","From automotive production lines supplying international markets to artificial intelligence solutions reaching across continents, Tunisia is increasingly competing on what it creates and the skills it can offer.",yes,no,0,10
