Senegal,Macroeconomy,Senegal bonds fall after Sonko opposes budget bills,https://www.cnbcafrica.com/2026/senegal-bonds-fall-after-sonko-opposes-budget-bills,CNBC Africa,21 Oct 2026,,no,"DAKAR/JOHANNESBURG (Reuters) – Senegal’s international bonds fell sharply on Tuesday after National Assembly President Ousmane Sonko said lawmakers would not back budget legislation, raising fresh doubts over how quickly the government can push ahead with its debt rework.","All of Senegal’s euro- and dollar-denominated bond maturities fell more than a cent on the day, with longer-dated debt suffering the sharpest losses. The 2037 bond dropped 2.166 cents to bid at 48.931 cents on the euro, Tradeweb data showed.","Sonko remains one of Senegal’s most powerful political figures despite being fired as prime minister by President Bassirou Diomaye Faye in May. He leads the ruling PASTEF party, which controls 130 of parliament’s 165 seats, and was elected speaker with the backing of 132 lawmakers, giving him significant influence over Faye’s legislative agenda.",yes,no,1,14
