Senegal,Digital Economy,Africa emerges as D2D satellite battleground,https://itweb.africa/article/africa-emerges-as-d2d-satellite-battleground/KA3WwMdzXjNvrydZ,ITWeb Africa,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Direct-to-device (D2D) satellite connectivity is emerging as the next battleground for satellite companies targeting Africa, as the race to connect the continent’s most underserved communities gathers pace.","While the technology promises to overcome traditional infrastructure limitations by linking standard smartphones directly to satellites, its success will depend on regulatory hurdles, affordability and competition from local operators.","According to the GSMA Intelligence Satellite and NTN tracker, Q3 2026 , sub-Saharan Africa has the lowest share of mobile operators with satellite partnerships globally, at 13%, compared with the worldwide average of 19%. However, commercial D2D deployments are beginning to take shape.",yes,no,2,8
