Botswana,Macroeconomy,"Botswana, China open new chapter in longstanding friendship with elevated ties: Botswanan president",https://en.people.cn/n3/2026/1026/c90000-20512254.html,People's Daily Online,21 Oct 2026,,no,"China's zero-tariff treatment for African countries is creating new opportunities for South African exporters, manufacturers and small businesses to expand into the Chinese market, while strengthening calls for more balanced trade, local industrial development and job creation, officials said at a briefing reception in Pretoria on Thursday.","The event, held at the CT Hotel, brought together South Africa's Minister of Trade, Industry and Competition, Parks Tau, Chinese Ambassador to South Africa Wu Peng, South African Revenue Service (SARS) Interim Deputy Commissioner Schalk Human, government officials and business representatives to discuss the implementation of China's zero-tariff policy and its practical implications for South African businesses.","The policy, which took effect on May 1, 2026, extends zero-tariff treatment to 53 African countries that maintain diplomatic relations with China. South African products that meet the applicable rules of origin can enter the Chinese market without customs duties, subject to the scheme's provisions and specified tariff-rate quotas. The arrangement is scheduled to run until April 30, 2028.",yes,no,3,7
