Botswana,Governance,BCP builds momentum ahead of 2029 polls,https://www.mmegi.bw/news/bcp-builds-momentum-ahead-of-2029-polls/news,Mmegi Online,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Despite losing three by-elections, officials told journalists this week that the party recorded an increase in the number of people voting in comparison with its performance in the last General Election. BCP president, Dumelang Saleshando, stated that the figures should not be dismissed at face value, insisting that the party's performance reflected its continued growth and strengthening grassroots structures. “We do not take those numbers lightly, and it even helps us to strengthen structures as BCP,” he said at a media briefing on Tuesday at Travel Lodge following their triumph in Sefhophe by-election.","“That alone clearly shows that the BCP is growing, and there is no doubt that we will [be ready for] the 2029 General Elections.” He maintained that increasing voter support in by-elections is significant for an opposition party, adding such gains demonstrated the BCP's ability to consolidate its political base, even reflected what he described as growing public dissatisfaction with the Umbrella for Democratic Change (UDC) government. According to Saleshando, voters are beginning to recognise that their decision to elect the UDC had been a mistake, arguing that the government is struggling to provide clear direction. The BCP president suggested that the political landscape is shifting, with voters increasingly assessing the performance of the governing party rather than simply remaining loyal to their previous electoral choices. Beyond the changing political mood, Saleshando raised concerns about the growing influence of money in electoral campaigns, saying the use of financial incentives to attract voters has become an increasingly troubling feature of Botswana's politics.",,yes,no,4,6
