Botswana,Agrifood & Climate,Southern Africa El Niño Drought Response,https://www.wvi.org/newsroom/south-africa/southern-africa-prepares-anticipated-impacts-el-nino-202627,World Vision International (WVI),21 Oct 2026,,no,Southern Africa prepares for the Anticipated Impacts of El Niño 2026/27,"The Southern African Development Community (SADC) today opened the 2026 Disaster Preparedness and Response Planning Workshop in Johannesburg, South Africa, under the theme, “From Forecast to Consequence: Anticipating the Cascading Impacts of El Niño 2026/27 in Southern Africa.” The four-day workshop is convened by the SADC Secretariat in collaboration with the European Union, through the European Commission’s Directorate-General for European Civil Protection and Humanitarian Aid Operations (DG ECHO), and in partnership with the Regional Anticipatory Action Working Group (RAAWG). Participating partners include the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO), the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC), the International Organization for Migration (IOM), Start Network, the United Nations Children’s Fund (UNICEF), the World Food Programme (WFP), the World Health Organization (WHO) and World Vision.","The workshop focuses on strengthening preparedness, advancing anticipatory action and enhancing coordination in response to the potential impacts of El Niño during the 2026/2027 rainfall season. The discussions are aimed at ensuring that governments and humanitarian actors are better positioned to anticipate emerging risks, mobilise resources and implement timely interventions to protect vulnerable communities and safeguard livelihoods.",yes,no,3,7
Botswana,Agrifood & Climate,"Edo to partner Botswana on agric, livestock development",https://punchng.com/edo-to-partner-botswana-on-agric-livestock-development/,Punch Newspapers,25 Oct 2026,,no,The Edo State Government is seeking Botswana’s partnership in agriculture and livestock development as part of efforts to attract foreign investment ahead of its forthcoming International Agricultural and Livestock Investment Summit.,"The state government made the appeal during a meeting with the Botswana High Commissioner to Nigeria, Philada Kereng, at the country’s High Commission in Abuja on Friday.","The delegation was led by the Edo State Commissioners for Agriculture and Food Security, Dr Jerry Uwangue, and Livestock Development, Mr Ohimai Ehijimetor.",yes,no,4,10
