Equatorial Guinea,Digital Economy,National Bank of Ethiopia connects to PAPSS payments network,https://www.fintechfutures.com/cross-border-payments/national-bank-of-ethiopia-connects-to-papss-network,FinTech Futures,19 Oct 2026,,no,The National Bank of Ethiopia (NBE) has joined the Pan-African Payment and Settlement System (PAPSS) network.,"PAPSS was launched in 2022 by Egypt-based Afreximbank with the purpose of streamlining cross-border payments between countries across Africa. Since its establishment, PAPSS has now grown to connect 29 African countries, enabling more than 190 commercial banks and fintechs to transact across the continent.","Commenting on the milestone, Dr Eyob Tekalign, governor of the National Bank of Ethiopia, says: ""Ethiopia’s integration into the PAPSS network represents an important step in our continued efforts to modernise our financial system and deepen our economic connections with the rest of Africa. It creates new opportunities for Ethiopian financial institutions and businesses to participate more actively in cross-border payments and intra-African trade.""",yes,no,3,7
