Sierra Leone,Jobs & Employment,Sierra Leone Launches National Shipping Carrier with Chinese Support,https://maritime-executive.com/article/sierra-leone-launches-national-shipping-carrier-with-chinese-support,The Maritime Executive,23 Oct 2026,,no,"With governments across Africa planning to grow domestic fleets, Sierra Leone has moved ahead by establishing a national shipping company. President Julius Maada Bio presided last week over the launch at the Queen Elizabeth II Quay in the country’s port city and capital, Freetown. The establishment of the national carrier is part of the wider maritime sector reforms being undertaken by the government.","The backdrop to the ceremony was the Chinese-owned bulker XH Explorer (176,298 dwt). The vessel, built in 2003, and registered in Liberia, is managed from Singapore and has been running between Sierra Leone and Asia.","In recent months, key legislative instruments have been passed, including the Revised Merchant Shipping Act 2026 and the Maritime Pollution Bill. Among these new laws was also the Sierra Leone National Shipping Agency (SLNSA) Act 2025. The law effectively transformed the old Sierra Leone National Shipping Company (SLNSC) into the Sierra Leone National Shipping Agency (SLNSA).",yes,no,2,8
