Central African Republic,Agrifood & Climate,How El Niño is driving hunger and drought across Central America,https://www.wfp.org/stories/how-el-nino-driving-hunger-and-drought-across-central-america,UN World Food Programme,22 Oct 2026,,no,"During my travels across Central America in recent months, I have witnessed how drought driven by El Niño has evolved from a distant threat to reality and, today, an emergency.","The farmers of a small agricultural cooperative in the northern community of San Diego, Nicaragua, whom I met at the end of April, had no doubts: rainfall prospects were bleak, even by the standards of Central America's Dry Corridor. Rising fertilizer prices, up by nearly 50 percent since the beginning of the year, darkened the outlook.","Those predictions were soon confirmed. By July, in Jalapa, Guatemala, farmers guided me through plots where crops had barely reached half their normal height. And by the time I arrived in Honduras in early September, communities and authorities were already sounding the alarm: dry wells and rivers, failed harvests and dead livestock.",yes,no,0,10
