Kenya,Digital Economy,Kenya Partners With South Korea to Boost Artificial Intelligence in Public Services,https://www.dawan.africa/news/kenya-partners-with-south-korea-to-boost-artificial-intelligence-in-public-services,Dawan Africa,21 Oct 2026,,no,"Kenya, October 21, 2026 - Kenya is taking a big step into the digital future by joining forces with South Korea to build smarter government systems. Leaders from both nations met at the Embassy of Kenya in Seoul to sign a new deal during the Global AI and Digital Summit. Cabinet Secretary for Information, Communication, and the Digital Economy William Kabogo witnessed the official signing of the agreement between Kenya's ICT Authority and the Korea Data Agency.","This partnership is all about using artificial intelligence, or smart computer tools, to make everyday government tasks faster and easier for citizens. Computers need organized information to learn, so team members will first work on preparing official records and testing new computer tools across public offices. This could mean faster services when people apply for official documents or seek help at public health centers.","Modern government offices rely heavily on digital systems to run smoothly, but these systems must talk to each other safely. Under this new plan, experts from South Korea will help train Kenyan data workers on how to organize records properly. They will also build safe networks to share information across government departments without risking anyone's privacy.",yes,no,4,6
