Kenya,Workforce & Human Capital,"“You can do it”: Catholic Bishops in Kenya Urge Focus, Hard Work as 3.6 Million Sit National Exams",https://www.aciafrica.org/news/24871/you-can-do-it-catholic-bishops-in-kenya-urge-focus-hard-work-as-36-million-sit-national-exams,ACI Africa,23 Oct 2026,,no,"Catholic Bishops in Kenya have urged candidates undertaking national examinations and assessments to remain focused and work hard, extending good wishes as some 3.6 million learners take part in this year’s exercise across the East African nation.","In a statement issued on Wednesday, October 21, members of the Kenya Conference of Catholic Bishops (KCCB), through its Commission for Education and Religious Education (CERE), encouraged candidates to pursue their academic goals.","“Best Wishes to all KCSE, KJSEA, KPSEA candidates in the 2026 national examinations and assessments. You can do it. Dream, focus, work hard, succeed,” the KCCB statement reads in part, referring to the Kenya Certificate of Secondary Education, the Kenya Junior School Education Assessment, and the Kenya Primary School Education Assessment, respectively.",yes,no,3,7
