Mali,Workforce & Human Capital,Bulgaria: Teachers’ unions unite behind call to fund public education and strengthen the teaching profession,https://www.ei-ie.org/en/item/33177:bulgaria-teachers-unions-unite-behind-call-to-fund-public-education-and-strengthen-the-teaching-profession,Education International,20 Oct 2026,,no,"Education union leaders from across Southeast Europe gathered in Sofia, Bulgaria, for a three-day strategic forum under Education International’s (EI) Go Public! Fund Education campaign. The meeting focused on one of the most pressing challenges facing education systems worldwide: ensuring sustainable investment in public education and rebuilding the attractiveness of the teaching profession.","Hosted by the Bulgarian Teachers’ Union (SEB), the meeting brought together union representatives from Albania, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Kosovo, and Slovenia, alongside national education authorities and representatives from Education International and the European Trade Union Committee for Education (ETUCE). The forum provided an opportunity for participants to exchange experiences and develop common strategies to address the growing teacher shortage crisis, improve working conditions, strengthen social dialogue, and secure adequate funding for education.","Opening the forum, Yanka Takeva, SEB President, stressed the importance of recognising education as a strategic investment rather than a budgetary cost. She highlighted the need for policies that respond to changing social realities, technological transformation, demographic challenges, and evolving expectations of education systems.",yes,no,4,6
