Niger,Workforce & Human Capital,Niger State education ministry’s chaotic school calendar,https://thenationonlineng.net/niger-state-education-ministrys-chaotic-school-calendar/,The Nation Newspaper,22 Oct 2026,,no,"Sir: The management of education requires foresight, consistency, effective communication, and a clear commitment to students’ academic progress. Unfortunately, recurring disruptions to the school calendar in Niger State raise serious concerns about the performance of the Ministry of Basic and Secondary Education, the agency responsible for overseeing basic and secondary education in the state.",Why should students in Niger State repeatedly lose valuable learning time because of decisions that could have been better planned and communicated?,"In June, private schools were reportedly compelled to close one or two weeks earlier than schools in the Federal Capital Territory (FCT) and some other states, putting students under pressure to prepare for and take their examinations. In September, schools in Niger State, including private schools, were reportedly directed to delay resumption by one or two weeks after schools in other states and the FCT had resumed.",yes,no,3,7
