Somalia,Jobs & Employment,Somalia and Uganda Sign Labour Deal to Protect Workers' Rights,https://www.dawan.africa/news/somalia-and-uganda-sign-labour-deal-to-protect-workers-rights,Dawan Africa,22 Oct 2026,,no,"MOGADISHU, 22 October 2026 Somalia and Uganda have signed a bilateral labour agreement aimed at protecting workers’ rights and regulating employment, officials said on Thursday.","The agreement was signed by the two countries’ ministries responsible for labour during the Somalia-Uganda Joint Permanent Commission mid-term review, business forum and joint exhibition held in Mogadishu from 20 to 22 October.","Uganda’s Labour Minister Henry Tumukunde said the deal was intended to address challenges faced by some Ugandan workers in Somalia, including unpaid wages and employment benefits, the withholding of passports, employment without written contracts and disputes over work permits.",yes,no,1,9
