Somalia,Macroeconomy,Around the World: Somalia Plans First Currency in 35 Years,https://www.numismaticnews.net/around-the-world-somalia-plans-first-currency-in-35-years,Numismatic News,23 Oct 2026,,no,The dollar bill is estimated to last about six years in circulation . Can you imagine what a bank note would look like if it had to last for 35 years? That is the predicament that has happened in Somalia.,"The nation, which stretches across the Horn of Africa, suffered through a civil war between 1991 and 2006. The insurgency that followed the establishment of the Transitional Federal Government of Somalia continued through 2012. The constant warfare left Somalia as being one of the least developed nations on earth.","Currently, there is a Federal Government of Somalia, but insurgents continue to control parts of the beleaguered nation. Livestock and US currency function as money alongside 35-year-old Somali banknotes that are now increasingly being refused by merchants due to their ragged condition. So, why doesn’t Somalia simply arrange to have fresh banknotes printed?",yes,no,2,8
