Tunisia,Workforce & Human Capital,Why does Tunisia become African only when Europe needs it to be?,https://africasacountry.com/2026/10/why-does-tunisia-become-african-only-when-europe-needs-it-to-be,Africa Is a Country,23 Oct 2026,,no,"T unisia is an African country that has spent much of its modern political imagination looking north. That sounds like a question of identity. In reality, it is a question of power—and more precisely, a practice of domination through classification.","For decades, Tunisia has imagined its economic future through the Mediterranean: European markets, French education, tourism, and European investment. Africa has often appeared somewhere beyond the Sahara, associated with instability, migration, and security.","Europe, however, possesses its own geography of Tunisia—one that shifts depending on what Europe needs from it. When Brussels discusses trade, investment, and political cooperation, Tunisia is a Mediterranean neighbor. When Europe discusses migration, border control, Libya, or the Sahel, Tunisia becomes something else: an African frontier state.",yes,no,2,8
